# Idearium's build pipeline — James, 2026-11-08: "First one. Like pipelines." · "hooking in idearium. The pipeline in idearium is meant to be shown on the canvas.
# Gates are inbetween steps. So compartment, gate, compartment, gate." (OC9; AE_D7). Each step is an api step to nexus://idearium (COS routes it).
envelope: 1
uuid: nexus-export-pipeline-idearium-build
type: pipeline
id: idearium-build
context: Idearium › pipelines (served at GET /api/pipelines, run by COS)
intent: >-
  Idearium's build pipeline: what is ready, whether a phase already covers it, the phase mapped, its DAG whole, its graph, the build, closed on
  evidence, logged in the ledger. Each step calls Idearium by its own route (nexus://idearium); a gate stands after every step: compartment, gate,
  compartment, gate.
summary: 9 tasks · Idearium's own routes
system: idearium
tags:
  - pipeline
  - idearium
  - build
  - bundled
exported_at: 1794193416622
source: idearium/pipelines
occurrences: 1
payload:
  id: idearium-build
  format: nexus-pipeline
  version: 1
  name: Idearium build pipeline
  description: >-
    Idearium's build pipeline: what is ready, whether a phase already covers it, the phase mapped, its DAG whole, its graph, the build, closed on
    evidence, logged in the ledger. Each step calls Idearium by its own route (nexus://idearium); a gate stands after every step: compartment, gate,
    compartment, gate.
  vars:
    repo: nexus   # 2026-11-10: Nexus's own repo (Idearium reads "nexus" as it); another repo's uuid builds that repo
    phase: ''
    map: ''   # 2026-11-17: the phasemap of the phase, from the run form's list; a phase id can be in two maps (N1 is)
    files: ''
    does: ''
    why: ''
  settings:
    parallel: 1
  tasks:
    - id: ready
      label: What can be built now
      depends_on: []
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: nexus://idearium/api/phases/next
          method: GET
          timeoutMs: 120000   # 2026-11-17: a cold Idearium's census takes ~17 s and more under memory pressure; 30 s timed out (run 473c61df)
      gate: &ref_0
        contains: '"ok":true'
    - id: covered
      label: Does a phase already cover it
      depends_on:
        - ready
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: nexus://idearium/api/phases/ledger/covers
          method: POST
          body: '{"files":"{{vars.files}}","does":"{{vars.does}}"}'
      gate: *ref_0
    - id: map
      label: The phase is mapped
      depends_on:
        - covered
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: nexus://idearium/api/repos/{{vars.repo}}/phases/map
          method: GET
          timeoutMs: 120000
      gate: *ref_0
    - id: dag
      label: Its DAG is whole
      depends_on:
        - map
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: nexus://idearium/api/repos/{{vars.repo}}/phases/dag?phase={{vars.phase}}&map={{vars.map}}
          method: GET
          timeoutMs: 120000   # 2026-11-17: timed out at 30 s on a cold Idearium (run 11ac8139)
      gate: *ref_0
    - id: graph
      label: 'Its graph: files, crossings'
      depends_on:
        - dag
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: nexus://idearium/api/repos/{{vars.repo}}/phases/graph?phase={{vars.phase}}&map={{vars.map}}
          method: GET
          timeoutMs: 120000
      gate: *ref_0
    # 2026-11-18 (IF3 slice a) — James: "Yes, gates first". Before a build asks any model, the ready gate asks COS for its disk and memory:
    # short of either (his C: at 0 GB; DeepSeek leaving 3-5% RAM), the run holds here with the reason, no agent call spent; Continue asks again.
    - id: room
      label: Room to build (disk and memory)
      depends_on:
        - graph
      onFail: hold
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: nexus://idearium/health
          method: GET
          timeoutMs: 60000
      gate:
        type: ready
        with:
          minDiskMB: '2048'
          minFreeMemPct: '8'
    - id: build
      label: Build the phase
      depends_on:
        - room
      # 0.60.614 — James, 2026-11-20: "Like you can set the method or framework per gate or step. Remember the pipeline and gates are agnostic." ·
      # "framework per step. or pipeline. like i want it to use my framework." The method of each gate of this step, from his framework
      # (docs/innovation-toolkit.framework), resolved by COS (cos/automation/method.eg) and sent as {{vars.method}}. Which section serves which
      # gate is the coder's reading, to confirm with him; edit it here or on the canvas.
      method:
        diagnose:
          framework: innovation-toolkit
          steps:
            - gap
            - constraints
        test:
          framework: innovation-toolkit
          steps:
            - hostile
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: nexus://idearium/api/repos/{{vars.repo}}/phases/build
          method: POST
          body: '{"phase":"{{vars.phase}}","map":"{{vars.map}}","method":{{vars.method}}}'
          timeoutMs: 240000   # 0.60.494: the snapshot before a build took over 30 s once (run 78d4cc5a); the step gave up while Idearium was still starting it
      gate: *ref_0
    # 0.60.493 — James, 2026-11-11: "continue. get it working". The build step is met when the build has started; this one waits for it to end
    # and is met only when it landed. One ask waits up to 4 minutes (fetch gives up on a silent request at 5); a build still going is asked
    # again, 5 more times (about 24 minutes in all).
    # 2026-11-17 — his run ef902337 (N1): the build was still escalating (Claude answering) when the 6th ask came back "still building N1
    # (escalating); ask again", and the run failed with the build alive. His rule (2026-11-14): "persistence is non negiatiable until the
    # contract has been fullfilled". COS caps retries at 5 (cos/automation/pipeline.js), so a build still going after them HOLDS the run
    # (onFail: hold, 0.60.496) with Idearium's own reason ("still building … ask again"), instead of failing it; Continue asks again.
    - id: landed
      label: The build landed
      depends_on:
        - build
      retries: 5
      onFail: hold
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: nexus://idearium/api/repos/{{vars.repo}}/phases/landed?phase={{vars.phase}}&map={{vars.map}}&waitMs=240000
          method: GET
          timeoutMs: 280000
      gate: *ref_0
    # 0.60.496 — James, 2026-10-26: "the gate doesn't wait for me to accept it or not before it fails." A phase the evidence cannot close
    # (no test reaches it, a test failed, a file waits for his approval) holds the run here with the reason. He accepts or rejects the phase
    # in Idearium, then continues the run; the step is asked again.
    - id: evidence
      label: Closed on evidence
      depends_on:
        - landed
      onFail: hold
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: nexus://idearium/api/repos/{{vars.repo}}/phases/evidence
          method: POST
          body: '{"phase":"{{vars.phase}}","map":"{{vars.map}}","apply":true}'
          timeoutMs: 180000
      gate: *ref_0
    - id: ledger
      label: Logged in the phase ledger
      depends_on:
        - evidence
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: nexus://idearium/api/phases/ledger/log
          method: POST
          # 2026-11-18 — run 74f98418 (N1) closed on evidence, then this step failed "say why: a ledger line without a reason is noise":
          # the run form sends no why. The pipeline says its own reason when none was given (no commas: they split a filter's arguments).
          body: '{"phase":"{{vars.phase}}","event":"built","why":{{vars.why | default:built through the Idearium build pipeline and closed on evidence | json}},"by":"pipeline"}'
      gate: *ref_0
